  "title": "Dataset Clinical Epilepsy iEEG to BIDS - RESPect_longterm_iEEG",
  "description": "A clinical intracranial EEG (iEEG) dataset from 12 epilepsy surgery patients drawn from the RESPect (Registry for Epilepsy Surgery Patients) collection at the University Medical Center Utrecht. It includes six intraoperative ECoG recordings and six long-term recordings (three ECoG, three SEEG). The data are organized in BIDS, with session and run conventions that capture the surgical stage or the monitoring day and time, and the task labels describe the patient's state.",
  "methods_description": "Intraoperative ECoG was grouped into BIDS sessions by surgical situation (pre-resection, intermediate, post-resection) and grid position. Long-term monitoring recordings were grouped into sessions per monitoring period, with runs encoding the day and start time. Task labels (rest, sleep, SPESclin) describe the patient's state during each recording.",
